137	  <section>
138	    <h2>Patterns behind the entries</h2>
139	    <p class="note">The same few causes account for most of the register.</p>
140	    <div class="cols">
141	      <div><h3>Checked before the lock, written after</h3>
142	        <p>A value is validated on a copy loaded earlier and then written back. A double click or two staff on one record is enough to trigger it.</p>
143	        <p class="ref">FU-1, FU-3, FU-5, DO-4, DO-5, RR-2, TX-1, TX-5, ST-9</p></div>
144	      <div><h3>Read from the replica, written to the primary</h3>
145	        <p>Periodic tasks pick their work from the read replica and act on the primary without re-checking. Lag or an overlapping run repeats or misapplies the action.</p>
146	        <p class="ref">BT-2, BT-3, BT-4, BT-7, TX-14, WH-9</p></div>
147	      <div><h3>Zero treated as 'not given'</h3>
148	        <p>An amount of 0 falls through to a default, which in the refund paths is the full charged amount.</p>
149	        <p class="ref">RR-1, TX-7, DO-13</p></div>
150	      <div><h3>Ids not checked against their parent</h3>
151	        <p>A mutation takes an order plus line or transaction ids and never checks that they belong together, or that the staff member may act in that channel.</p>
152	        <p class="ref">FU-2, RR-3, RR-11, RR-12, TX-6</p></div>
153	      <div><h3>App failures that look like normal results</h3>
154	        <p>When a tax, shipping or payment app is slow or down, Saleor carries on with untaxed totals, unfiltered shipping methods, or a recorded 'failure' for an action that may have happened.</p>
155	        <p class="ref">DO-6, WH-6, TX-4, WH-7</p></div>
156	      <div><h3>States with no way out</h3>
157	        <p>Several records can end up pending with no retry, edit or delete available to staff, and nothing that sweeps them up.</p>
